.TH "zbuild" "1" "2026\-11\-04"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
zbuild \- Incremental compilation driver for the Zoril language
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBzbuild\fR [\fIoptions\fR] <entry.\&zrl>
.br
\fBzbuild\fR \fB\-\-gc\fR [\fB\-\-cache\-dir\fR <dir>]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBzbuild\fR is the incremental compilation driver for the Zoril systems programming language.\& It orchestrates the multi\-stage compilation pipeline (\fBzoril\fR(1), \fBzilc\fR(1), \fBqbe\fR(1), \fBas\fR(1), and \fBld\fR(1)) across the complete dependency graph reachable from the entry module.\&
.PP
.SH COMPILATION CACHE AND INCREMENTAL REBUILDS
.PP
\fBzbuild\fR caches compiled intermediate objects and interface summaries inside the build cache directory (by default \fB.\&zoril\-cache\fR in the current working directory).\& Rebuild decisions are computed using cryptographic SHA\-256 hashes of module interfaces rather than file modification timestamps alone.\& When an upstream module changes without modifying its public interface, downstream modules that depend on it are not recompiled.\&
.PP
At the conclusion of a build, \fBzbuild\fR reports the compilation volume:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
compiled: N modules
.fi
.RE
.PP
If no dependencies or source files have changed since the previous build, \fBzbuild\fR reports \fBcompiled: 0 modules\fR and links the existing cached artifacts directly.\&
.PP
.SH MODULE RESOLUTION
.PP
When a source file executes \fBimport "foo.\&zrl"\fR, \fBzbuild\fR searches for the imported module in the following order:
1.\& Relative to the importing source file'\&s directory.\&
2.\& In include directories specified with \fB\-I\fR in left\-to\-right order.\&
3.\& In the project root directory specified with \fB\-\-root\fR.\&
4.\& In the installed standard library directory (discovered relative to the \fBzbuild\fR
binary at \fB.\&.\&/share/zoril/stdlib\fR).\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Display usage summary and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Display version information and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-o\fR <path>
.RS 4
Set the output executable path.\& Defaults to \fB.\&/a.\&out\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-I\fR <dir>
.RS 4
Add an include directory to the module search path.\& Repeatable.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-root\fR <dir>
.RS 4
Set the project root directory.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cache\-dir\fR <dir>
.RS 4
Specify an alternative build cache directory.\& Defaults to \fB.\&zoril\-cache\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-gc\fR
.RS 4
Garbage\-collect the build cache.\& When invoked without an entry module, \fBzbuild\fR removes database records whose source files no longer exist on disk and deletes unreferenced object and interface artifacts.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
.RS 4
Enable detailed progress output, reporting cache hits, misses, and execution of underlying pipeline tools.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-compiler\fR <path>
.RS 4
Explicit path to the \fBzoril\fR(1) compiler frontend binary.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-zilc\fR <path>
.RS 4
Explicit path to the \fBzilc\fR(1) intermediate lowerer binary.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-qbe\fR <path>
.RS 4
Explicit path to the QBE code generator binary.\& Overrides \fBBACKEND_BIN\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-as\fR <path>
.RS 4
Explicit path to the system assembler binary.\& Overrides \fBASSEMBLER_BIN\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-ld\fR <path>
.RS 4
Explicit path to the system linker binary.\& Overrides \fBLINKER_BIN\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-hosted\fR
.RS 4
Build a program that is linked into a libc process: the compiler is run with \fB\-\-hosted\fR, the link goes through \fBcc\fR with \fBruntime_hosted.\&o\fR instead of \fBld\fR with \fBruntime.\&o\fR, and the linker is given only \fBPATH\fR as its environment.\& The flag is part of the toolchain id, so objects built with and without it are never reused for each other.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-cc\fR <path>
.RS 4
The C compiler driver that links a \fB\-\-hosted\fR program.\& Overrides \fBLINK_CC\fR; defaults to \fBcc\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-link\-object\fR <file>
.RS 4
Link this object file (a C object, say) into the program, after the program'\&s own objects.\& Repeatable.\& A file that does not exist is an error naming it.\& \fB\-\-link\-object\fR, \fB\-L\fR, \fB\-l\fR and \fB\-\-link\-arg\fR reach the linker in the order they are given.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-L\fR <dir>
.RS 4
Add a library search directory to the link.\& Repeatable.\& \fB\-L\fR<dir> is also accepted.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-l\fR <name>
.RS 4
Link the library \fBlib\fR<name> (\fBlib\fR<name>\fB.\&a\fR or \fBlib\fR<name>\fB.\&so\fR).\& Repeatable.\& \fB\-l\fR<name> is also accepted.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-link\-arg\fR <arg>
.RS 4
Pass <arg> to the linker as it is.\& Repeatable.\& Link inputs reach the final link only: changing one relinks the program and recompiles no module.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-runtime\fR <path>
.RS 4
Path to the Zoril runtime assembly object (\fBruntime.\&o\fR).\& By default, \fBzbuild\fR locates the runtime relative to its own binary at \fB.\&.\&/lib/zoril/runtime.\&o\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-checked\fR
.RS 4
Developer option, not a user\-facing mode: build the program with \fBzoril \-\-checked\fR, which instruments it for memory\-safety testing.\& The mode is part of the toolchain id, so objects built with and without it are never reused for each other.\& A release build is unaffected.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-provenance\fR, \fB\-\-provenance=warn\fR
.RS 4
Developer option: compile every module with \fBzoril \-\-provenance\fR (or \fB=warn\fR), the origin\-set store and return rules.\& Part of the toolchain id, so an object compiled without the rules is never reused with them.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
\fBBACKEND_BIN\fR
.RS 4
Default path to the QBE backend binary (default: \fBqbe\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBASSEMBLER_BIN\fR
.RS 4
Default path to the system assembler binary (default: \fBas\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBLINKER_BIN\fR
.RS 4
Default path to the system linker binary (default: \fBld\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBLINK_CC\fR
.RS 4
Default C compiler driver for linking a \fB\-\-hosted\fR program (default: \fBcc\fR).\&
.PP
.RE
.SH CURRENT LIMITS
.PP
\fBzbuild\fR links Zoril modules with the assembly runtime object (\fBld\fR, no libc), or with \fB\-\-hosted\fR into a libc process (\fBcc\fR).\& C objects, libraries and linker arguments are added with \fB\-\-link\-object\fR, \fB\-L\fR, \fB\-l\fR and \fB\-\-link\-arg\fR.\& It does not read a project file, and it builds for Linux x86_64 only.\&
.PP
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
\fB0\fR
.RS 4
Build or cache operation completed successfully.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB1\fR
.RS 4
A compilation, linking, or dependency resolution error occurred.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Build an application executable:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
cat << \&'EOF\&' > main\&.zrl
import "io\&.zrl";
use io::println;

fn main() \-> i32 {
    println("Hello from zbuild!");
    return 0;
}
EOF

zbuild \-o app main\&.zrl
\&./app
.fi
.RE
.PP
Clean obsolete build artifacts from the cache:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
zbuild \-\-gc
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBzoril\fR(1), \fBzilc\fR(1), \fBzoril\-stdlib\fR(7)
